 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Outside the police station, Max tries to swap toddlers with Nastya's baffled father, while back at the restaurant Chef Barinov and Fedya heave the safe out the window.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Ну вот ваш Степан.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Давай сделаем обмен.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Это совсем другой мальчик.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Дети не могут так быстро меняться.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Снимите маску и посмотрите.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Где же тогда мой внук?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Подняли сейф, осторожно!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Справа аккуратно обходим стол.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Шеф, помогли бы нам лучше!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Вообще-то я этим и занимаюсь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Давай сюда, тяни на себя.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Всё, нам конец!",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's go through each line of the toddler swap and the safe disaster.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Ну вот ваш Степан.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Well, here is your Stepan.' Max presents the real grandson using the demonstrative particle 'here is'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Давай сделаем обмен.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Let's make a swap.' The noun for 'exchange' or 'swap' is the direct object of 'let's make'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Это совсем другой мальчик.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'This is a completely different boy.' The adverb 'completely' intensifies the adjective 'other/different'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Дети не могут так быстро меняться.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Children cannot change that fast.' The reflexive infinitive means 'to change' in appearance or character.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Снимите маску и посмотрите.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Take off the mask and take a look.' Polite plural imperatives urge the skeptical grandfather to check the boy's face.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Где же тогда мой внук?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Where is my grandson then?' Once the mask comes off, the grandfather demands to know where his real grandson is.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Подняли сейф, осторожно!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We lifted the safe, careful!' The adverb 'carefully' serves as a quick warning cry while carrying something heavy.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Справа аккуратно обходим стол.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We go around the table carefully on the right.' The prefix 'ob-' on the motion verb means 'to walk around' an obstacle.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Шеф, помогли бы нам лучше!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Chef, you could help us instead!' Combining the past tense with the conditional particle turns a wish into a mild reproach: 'you might have helped'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "chef",
   "t": "Вообще-то я этим и занимаюсь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Actually, that is exactly what I am doing.' The conversational opener means 'actually' or 'as a matter of fact'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Давай сюда, тяни на себя.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Bring it this way, pull toward yourself.' In Russian, 'pull toward yourself' is also how doors are labeled 'Pull'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Всё, нам конец!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'That is it, we are done for!' When the safe smashes onto German's car below, Fedya sums up their doom with 'to us is the end'. Now let's hear the whole sequence again at natural speed.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
